message:
test(boot-window): register the load-bearing mutations as durable claims

The mutation runs behind BW-0/H2/H3 were ad-hoc. Six of them belong in the
repo's own `scripts/changed_line_mutation_check.py` registry so they re-run
against any future diff that touches the same lines, rather than living only in a
commit message:

- a named import segment stamped as a plausible constant;
- an unmeasured segment fabricating 0 instead of being absent;
- the bytecode sweep losing its single-winner lock;
- an unlockable checkout losing the stale-bytecode guard entirely (the
  regression BW-H2's first draft actually had);
- the deferred `model_tools` import returning to module scope;
- the registry being read before the deferred import populates it (the silent
  "this persona has no tools" answer BW-H3's first draft actually had).

`--base main` selects 5 of the 6 against this branch (the sixth's anchor line is
a deletion, which the changed-line selector cannot see) and kills all 5, exit 0.

